        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/pr_review_gate.py:690-696 maps RETROSPECTIVE_REFRESH to \"terminal-reconciliation\" and calls winning_claim with a job that has no `refresh`. job_id() now appends `:f<key>` (lifecycle_workers.py job_id). So an unexpired claim on the keyed terminal job is not detected, and the operator can re-offer while a worker still holds it. The same missing key at pr_review_gate.py:724-728 makes the last-outcome lookup return \"unknown\" instead of the stale-block receipt. Nothing in the tests e",
